 # The `standard` agent preset: the full coding agent, mounted once per process.
 #
+# ── the kernel switch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+#
+# `kernel.enabled` in the user's settings document picks between two rosters,
+# and several rows below read it through `dshSettingFlag('kernel.enabled', true)`.
+#
+#   ON  (default) — the model acts through `kernel`, a persistent Python
+#                   namespace. Reading a file, editing it, searching the tree,
+#                   running a command are function calls inside it, so the shell,
+#                   filesystem, search, and background-job rows switch OFF.
+#   OFF           — those rows switch ON and the kernel switches off: the
+#                   conventional roster, exactly as this preset shipped.
+#
+# Only the rows the kernel REPLACES move. Web access, delegation, skills, goals,
+# planning, todos, and asking the user are mounted either way — the kernel
+# cannot do any of them, so switching them off would cost capability and buy
+# nothing.
+#
+# The switch is read once at boot, which is why it is a Loader `disabled`
+# expression rather than a value some plugin re-reads. A tool's prompt section
+# is registered when its plugin mounts, so a tool merely hidden at runtime would
+# leave its instructions in the system prompt describing a tool the model cannot
+# call. Mounting is the only gate that takes the instructions with it. Changing
+# the switch therefore needs a restart, and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-kernel-mode`
+# declares `applies: 'restart'` so the settings UI says so.
+#
 # This file is an AGENT-PLANE composition. The roster mounts it ONCE under a
 # standing scope; every session naming it joins by scope parentage, so the
 # tools and prompt sections registered here cover each joined agent while a
@@ -41,23 +66,43 @@
